WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.418
Internal network abuse occurs when user-controlled input influences a server-side request.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:14.328
Features such as URL previews, webhook testing, file import, and document conversion may reach systems that attackers cannot access directly.

3
00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:17.531
Metadata service attacks are common in cloud environments.

4
00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:25.304
If a workload can reach metadata endpoints, attackers may attempt to obtain temporary credentials or environmental details.

5
00:00:25.304 --> 00:00:30.532
Trust boundary violations happen when applications treat user-supplied destinations as safe.

6
00:00:30.532 --> 00:00:37.786
URL allowlists, protocol restrictions, DNS handling, and redirect controls must be designed carefully.

7
00:00:37.786 --> 00:00:49.889
SSRF defenses work best when application validation is paired with network segmentation, egress filtering, boundary protection, and monitoring for unusual server-initiated traffic.

8
00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:52.912
Use network segmentation and boundary protection.

9
00:00:52.912 --> 00:00:56.305
Restrict destinations with URL allowlists where possible.

10
00:00:56.305 --> 00:01:01.044
Apply egress filtering and monitor unusual server-initiated requests.

